course: dictionary
lesson: 9636
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one to use. Read the sentence around the word and ask which meaning fits best.
explain: «Each ring in a tree stump is one year of growth.» Here a stump is the short part of a tree left in the ground after the tree is cut down.
explain: «A hard question stumps the class.» Here stumps is a verb: the question is so hard that nobody can answer it. The sentence gives the clue, because a class cannot count rings on a question.
fact: A stump is the short part of a tree left in the ground after the tree is cut down.
fact: In cricket, the stumps are the three upright sticks that make the wicket.
fact: To stump someone is to ask them something so hard they cannot answer.
fact: Each ring in a tree stump is one year of growth: wide rings show good years, and thin rings show dry or cold years.
exercise: «Each ring in a tree stump is one year of growth.» What is a stump here? | A kind of bird | A tall tree with many branches | *The short part of a tree left in the ground after it is cut down | A small green plant
exercise: In cricket, the bowler tries to hit the stumps. What are the stumps? | Heavy steps that stamp | *Three upright sticks that make the wicket | Lines of rings in a tree | Twigs on a branch
exercise: «A hard question stumps the class.» What does stumps mean here? | Cuts down a tree | Glows in the dark | *Asks something so hard nobody can answer | Walks with heavy, stamping steps
test: «The potoo sits still on a branch looking exactly like a dead stump.» What does the potoo look like? | *A dead stump | A glowing lamp | A flying kite | A pink flower
test: «Wide rings show good years, thin rings show dry or cold years.» What do thin rings show? | Years with a lot of wind | Good years for growth | Years when the tree was cut down | *Dry or cold years
exam: «At first it's fun: twigs crackle, logs trip him, fungus on stumps looks like funny faces.» In this sentence, what are the stumps? | *Old tree stumps left in the ground | Cricket sticks | Walking sticks | Stumps of pencils
